			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync submodules to update Tauri baseline and centralize Rust lint rules\n\nSynchronize the `Dependency` and `Element` submodules to their latest revisions on the `Current` branch to align with upstream updates and internal build standardization.\n\nThe `Dependency` update advances the Tauri ecosystem to v2.11.2, migrating plugin bindings (Autostart, Store, WindowState) to v2 API signatures and updating tooling to TypeScript v6 and Vite v8. This ensures the Mountain backend's IPC mechanisms remain compatible with the latest stable Tauri release.\n\nThe `Element` update consolidates Rust lint suppression directives (`non_snake_case`, `dead_code`) from source directories into `build.rs` files across all backend submodules (Air, Common, Echo, Grove, Mountain, Rest, SideCar). This follows the strict PascalCase enforcement for source code, ensuring build-time warnings for generated code or FFI bindings do not pollute the main application source, while keeping the codebase warning-free and maintaining strict naming conventions.\n\nThese updates maintain the integrity of the dependency tree and unify the build pipeline's linting strategy across the editor ecosystem.",
